From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:21:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: venc: report the accepted capture buffer size

S_FMT preserves a requested capture sizeimage above the calculated minimum,
and queue_setup requires buffers of that size. Return the stored size from
G_FMT too, so applications do not allocate smaller buffers after querying
the selected format.

Fixes: d162aea8f633 ("media: venus: venc: amend buffer size for bitstream plane")
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index bd47bec9a6..20ea5e4c81 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -321,6 +321,7 @@ static int venc_g_fmt(struct file *file, void *fh, struct v4l2_format *f)
 		pixmp->colorspace = inst->colorspace;
 		pixmp->ycbcr_enc = inst->ycbcr_enc;
 		pixmp->quantization = inst->quantization;
+		pixmp->plane_fmt[0].sizeimage = inst->output_buf_size;
 		pixmp->xfer_func = inst->xfer_func;
 	} else if (f->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE) {
 		pixmp->width = inst->out_width;
